If a clinician considers an opioid then the clinician should always consider the opioid cautiously.
If a clinician prescribes an opioid then the clinician should always prescribe the opioid cautiously.
If an opioid-risk-stratification-tool is available and has a risk-ruling-out-ability for a long-term-opioid-therapy and there is a clinician then it is recommended that the clinician does not overestimate the risk-ruling-out-ability.
